          %h2#machine_implementation Machine implementation
          %p
            An important aspect of HoTT is the fact that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
            on which it is built has a computational implementation in proof assistants like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
          %p
            This forms the basis of the
            %em Univalent Foundations
            program (
            %a{:href => "#Voevodsky"}> Voevodsky
            ), which uses Coq to generate and verify proofs with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopical
            content.
          %p
            See the page
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formalized+libraries+of+homotopy+type+theory"} formalized libraries of homotopy type theory
            for more.
          %h2#DictionaryToCoq
            Dictionary HoTT-Coq /
            = succeed "-Category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            The following list displays some keywords defined in the
            = succeed "-implementation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            that they describe. (See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            and
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics+of+homotopy+type+theory"} categorical semantics of homotopy type theory
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a given ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            which
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                is
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally cartesian closed
            %li
              %p
                in addition has
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-colimits"} (∞,1)-colimits
          %p
            For instance
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            could be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            (in which case the homotopy type theory would be the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} internal language of an (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            Note that while Coq-HoTT is supposed to be the internal language for such
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em
              strict
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            for it are actually
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-categories"} 1-categories
            equipped with extra structure (such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+fibrant+objects"} categories of fibrant objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} presentations
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p We then have the following dictionary.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+types"} type of types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Type"} Type
          %pre
            %code Type
          %p
            denotes an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object+classifier"} object classifier
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            for a certain size of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
            have systems to manage universe sizes and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe+enlargement"} universe enlargement
            automatically; Agda’s is more advanced (universe polymorphism), whereas Coq’s is good enough for many purposes but tends to produce “universe inconsistencies” when working with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalence
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            Type (in the empty
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
          %pre
            %code X : Type
          %p
            denotes an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            in the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            by a model category or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system"} weak factorization system
            %em fibrant
            object.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
          %pre
            %code unit : Type
          %p
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} terminal object
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in C
            two objects, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} function type
          %pre
            %code X -&gt; Y : Type
          %p
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,Y] \in C
            (a formal proof of that fact is
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/guillaumebrunerie/HoTT/blob/master/Coq/Limits/AdjunctionProdHom.v"} here
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            (that is, a type in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
          %pre
            %code x : X  |-  P x : Type
          %p
            denotes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            (regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
          %pre
            %code P : X -&gt; Type
          %p
            denotes the corresponding classifying map, via an internal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
          %p
            The total space object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            of this bundle – the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
            – is the type equivalently coded as any of the following.
          %pre
            %code
              :preserve
                { x : X  &  P x } : Type
                sigT (fun (x : X) => P x) : Type.
                sigT P : Type          %p
            The first one is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sugaring"} syntactic sugar
            for the second. The third is related to the second by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eta+expansion"} eta expansion
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
          %p One might expect to also call the dependent sum type
          %pre
            %code exists x : X, P x
          %p
            (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/existential+quantifier"} existential quantifier
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            implementation that keyword is reserved for the corresponding operation on Coq’s built-in universe
            = succeed "," do
              %code Prop
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-truncated"} (-1)-truncated
            types. In fact, arguably in HoTT
            %code exists
            should refer not to the dependent sum itself, but to the (-1)-truncation thereof (its
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bracket+type"} bracket type
          %p The type
          %pre
            %code forall x : X, P x
          %p
            denotes the object of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to X
            — that is, the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            of the bundle. (See the section
            %em
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/dependent+product#RelationToSpacesOfSections"} relation to spaces of sections
            there). It also denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+quantifier"} universal quantifier
            when acting on (-1)-truncated objects
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
          %pre
            %code f : \forall x : X, P x
          %p
            denotes therefore a particular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of this bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi f
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; P
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{f}}\nearrow&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;= &amp; X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Given a type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
          %pre
            %code
              :preserve
                paths X : X -> X -> Type
                Id X : X -> X -> Type          %p
            corresponds to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+morphism"} diagonal morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to X\times X
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+space+object"} path space object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^I
          %p
            The fact that there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} X^I
            given by the inclusion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            is reflected in the
            = succeed "-definition" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+type"} inductive type
            = succeed "," do
              %code paths
          %p
            Then for
            %code x y : X
            two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terms"} terms
            regarded as morphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            (also called the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
          %pre
            %code
              :preserve
                paths X x y : Type
                x ~~> y : Type
                x == y : Type          %p
            (the latter two make use of Coq’s ability to define new notations), denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                          %mi y
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi x
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi y
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  x \times_X y &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{x}}
                  \\\
                  {*} &amp;\stackrel{y}{\to}&amp;  X
                  }
          %p
            which in a presentation by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            is given (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi P
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi x
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi X
                            %mrow
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi y
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P_{x,y} X &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{x}}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; X^{\Delta[1]} &amp;\to&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  {*} &amp;\stackrel{y}{\to}&amp; X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Beware that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} path induction rule
            applies to
            %code paths X
            not to
            = succeed "." do
              %code paths X x y
          %p
            More generally, we can define arbitrary pullbacks. If
            %code f : A -&gt; C
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %code g : B -&gt; C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            of
            %code f
            and
            %code g
            is defined by
          %pre
            %code {a : A &amp; {b : B &amp; f a ~~&gt; g b}}
          %p
            together with the obvious projections to
            %code A
            and
            %code B
            and the homotopy between the composites. (a proof can be found
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/guillaumebrunerie/HoTT/blob/master/Coq/Limits/Pullbacks.v"} here
          %p
            Using
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+types"} higher inductive types
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushouts"} homotopy pushouts
            %code g : C -&gt; A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %code f : C -&gt; B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pushout"} homotopy pushout
            of
            %code f
            and
            %code g
            is defined by
          %pre
            %code
              :preserve
                Inductive hopushout :=
                  | inl : A -> hopushout
                  | inr : B -> hopushout
                  | glue : forall x : C, inl (g x) ~~> inr (f x).          %p
            together with the map
            = succeed "," do
              %code inl
            %code inr
            and the homotopy
            = succeed "." do
              %code glue
            %a{:href => "https://github.com/guillaumebrunerie/HoTT/blob/master/Coq/Limits/Pushout.v"} here
            for the proof)
