              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HofmannStreicherGroupoidInterpretation.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1093/oso/9780198501275.003.0008"} doi:10.1093/oso/9780198501275.003.0008
          %p
            Generalization of this to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} strict ∞-groupoids
            were discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Warren"}> Michael Warren
              ,
              %em
                The strict
                = succeed "-groupoid" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/~mwarren/Papers/makkaifest_preprint.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            The fact that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            in which the cofibrations are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
            provides a sound
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#AwodeyWarren07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Awodey"}> Steve Awodey
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Warren"} Michael Warren
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy theoretic models of identity types
              %strong 146
              1 (2009) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0709.0248"}> arXiv:0709.0248
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004108001783"} doi:10.1017/S0305004108001783
          %p and with more details in
          %ul
            %li#Warren
