              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1211.2851"} arXiv:1211.2851
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4171/jems/1050"} doi:10.4171/jems/1050
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
          %p
            The trickiest question in finding models of homotopy type theory is to validate the
            = succeed "." do
