            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} discrete ∞-groupoids
            (see also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+Kan+fibration"} universal Kan fibration
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Kapulkin"}> Chris Kapulkin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"} Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"} Vladimir Voevodsky
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Univalence in simplicial sets
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.2553"} arXiv:v
            %li#Streicher14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"}> Thomas Streicher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A model of type theory in simplicial sets: A brief introduction to Voevodsky’s homotopy type theory
                %strong 12
                1 (2014) 45-49 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jal.2013.04.001"}> doi:10.1016/j.jal.2013.04.001
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                (notes by
                = succeed "):" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Kapulkin"} Chris Kapulkin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fiber bundles and univalence
                %a{:href => "http://www.pitt.edu/~krk56/fiber_bundles_univalence.pdf"} link
          %p
            A discussion of univalence for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+presheaves"} categories of presheaves
            over an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+category"} inverse category
          %ul
            %li#Shulman12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
              ,
              %em The univalence axiom for inverse diagrams
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.3253"}> arXiv:1203.3253
              ).
          %p
            Proof that all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentations
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            which interpret (provide
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalent
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universes"} type universes
          %ul
            %li#Shulman19
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
              ,
              %em
                All
                = succeed "-toposes" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.07004"}> arXiv:1904.07004
              ).
          %p
            Discussion of univalence in various other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            presentations for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+sets"}> cubical sets
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+sets"} cellular sets
          %ul
            %li#Cisinski14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              %em Univalent universes for elegant models of homotopy types
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1406.0058"}> arXiv:1406.0058
              )
          %p
            Models in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+sets"} cubical sets
            inside
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+set+theory"} constructive set theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            are discussed in
          %ul
            %li#BezemCoquandHuber13
              %p
                Marc Bezem,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thierry+Coquand"} Thierry Coquand
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A model of type theory in cubical sets
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2014/4628/"} web
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2014/4628/pdf/7.pdf"} pdf
            %li#KaposiAltenkirch14
              %p
                Ambrus Kaposi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thorsten+Altenkirch"} Thorsten Altenkirch
                %em A syntax for cubical type theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://mazzo.li/dump/aim-kaposi-pres.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            A weaker version of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Awodey+conjecture"} Awodey conjecture
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} locally cartesian closed (∞,1)-categories
            is explicitly stated in
          %ul
            %li#Joyal11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              ,
              %em Remarks on homotopical logic
              Oberwolfach (2011) (
              %a{:href => "http://hottheory.files.wordpress.com/2011/06/report-11_2011.pdf#page=19"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            An application of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter+quotient"} filter quotient
            construction as a new method to construct further models of homotopy type theory is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Rasekh"}> Nima Rasekh
              ,
              %em Non-Standard Models of Homotopy Type Theory
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/2508.07736"}> 2508.07736
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            See also the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory"} relation between type theory and category theory
          %h3#syntax Syntax
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicola+Gambino"}> Nicola Gambino
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"} Richard Garner
                %em The identity type weak factorisation system
                , Theoretical Computer Science 409 (2008), no. 3, pages 94–109.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"}> Richard Garner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benno+van+den+Berg"} Benno van den Berg
                %em Types are weak ω-groupoids
                ,
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"}> Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
                ,
                %em Weak ω-Categories from Intensional Type Theory
                , TLCA 2009, Brasília, Logical Methods in Computer Science, Vol. 6, issue 23, paper 24.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"}> Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
                ,
                %em Higher Categories from Type Theories
                , PhD Thesis: Carnegie Mellon University, 2010. [PDF]
            %li
              %p
                Michael Hedberg,
                %em A coherence theorem for Martin-Löf’s type theory
                , Journal of Functional Programming 8 (4): 413–436, July 1998.
          %h3#Code Code
          %p
            The basic
            = succeed "-code" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
            and the resulting homotopy type theory are at
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"}> Vladimir Voevodsky
                ,
                %em Experimental library of univalent formalization of mathematics
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0053"}> arXiv:1401.0053
                )
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/UniMath/"} github
            %li
              %p
                %em> The HoTT Library: A formalization of homotopy type theory in Coq
                , Andrej Bauer, Jason Gross, Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine, Mike Shulman, Matthieu Sozeau, Bas Spitters, 2016
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.04591"} arxiv
                and on
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT/wiki"} github
          %p A slightly more human readable version is collected as a single pdf in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em HoTT-Coq code
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HoTT-Coq-code.pdf", :title => "HoTT-Coq-code.pdf"}> HoTT-Coq-code.pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                Voevodsky, Vladimir and Ahrens, Benedikt and Grayson, Daniel and others,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unimath"} UniMath
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/UniMath"} GitHub
                link.
          %div
            %h3#HomotopyTheoryInHomotopyTyepTheoryReferences Homotopy theory formalized in homotopy type theory
            %p
              The following is a list of topics and results of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              that have been
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+logic"} formalized
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %p
              %br/
            %p
              On
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} homotopy groups of spheres
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+of+spheres+in+HoTT"} homotopy groups of spheres in HoTT
            %p
              On
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead%27s+theorem"} Whitehead's theorem
            %ul
              %li
                Dan’s proof for
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/dlicata335/hott-agda/blob/master/homotopy/Whitehead.agda"} n-types
            %p
              On
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spaces"} Eilenberg-MacLane spaces
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Dan’s
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "https://github.com/dlicata335/hott-agda/blob/master/homotopy/KGn.agda"} construction
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(G,n)
                  is a spectrum,
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT-Agda/blob/master/homotopy/EilenbergMacLane.agda"} formalized
            %p
              On
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT-Agda/blob/master/cohomology/SpectrumModel.agda"} Deriving cohomology theories from spectra
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT-Agda/blob/master/cohomology/MayerVietoris.agda"}> Mayer-Vietoris sequence
                  , with
                  %a{:href => "http://www.contrib.andrew.cmu.edu/~ecavallo/works/mayer-vietoris.pdf"} exposition
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT-Agda/blob/master/cohomology/Torus.agda"}> Cohomology of the n-torus
                  , which could be easily extended to any finite product of spheres.
              %li
                %p to do:
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      cohomology with finite coefficients, all we need is the boring work of defining
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
                      as an explicit group.
                  %li
                    %p Calculate some more cohomology groups.
                  %li
                    %p
                      Compute the loop space of
                      %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT-Agda/blob/master/homotopy/SpaceFromGroups.agda"} this construction
                      and use it to define spectra.
            %p
              On the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freudenthal+suspension+theorem"} Freudenthal suspension theorem
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Implies
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_k(S^n) = \pi_{k+1}(S^{n+1})
                  whenever
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \leq 2n - 2
              %li
                %p
                  Peter’s encode/decode-style proof,
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/dlicata335/hott-agda/blob/master/homotopy/Freudenthal.agda"} formalized
                  by Dan, using a clever lemma about maps out of 2 n-connected types. This is the “95%” version, which shows that the relevant map is an equivalence on truncations.
              %li
                %p
                  The full “100%” version,
                  %a{:href => "https://github.com/dlicata335/hott-agda/blob/master/homotopy/FreudenthalConnected.agda"} formalized
                  by Dan, which shows that the relevant map is
                  = succeed "-connected." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n
            %p
              On
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            %ul
              %li
                Jeremy Avigad, Chris Kapulkin and Peter Lumsdaine
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1304.0680"} arXiv
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/peterlefanulumsdaine/hott-limits/"} Coq code
            %p
              On the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/van+Kampen+theorem"} van Kampen theorem
            %ul
              %li
                Mike’s proofs are in the book and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://hott.github.com/HoTT-Agda/Homotopy.VanKampen.html"} Favonia formalized it
            %p
              On
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering+spaces"} covering spaces
            %ul
              %li Favonia’s proofs (link in flux due to library rewrite).
            %p
              On
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Blakers-Massey+theorem"} Blakers-Massey theorem
            %ul
              %li Favonia/Peter/Guillaume/Dan’s formalization of Peter/Eric/Dan’s proof (link in flux due to library rewrite).
        .revisedby
